Z||000000||Philphine||12-06-2000||09:38 PM||||ok... so it was just some thing i noticed. got enough snow sat. night to cover the car but the streets were pretty clear. drove to work (drill weekend)at a pretty good speed and when i got there looked at my hood. the spots behind where my hood vents are were clear and dry which proves...well...not much i guess but it does seem like the vents are having a positive effect on releasing air in the radiator area.<P>i may have mentioned it before, but since i can't do pics let me say my vents are the same as bbbadgt's side vents. they're from an '81 camaro z-28. <p>[This message has been edited by Philphine (edited 12-06-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000001||Uaana||12-07-2000||03:02 AM||||Another thing noticed once we got enough snow to notice. <BR>The rear wing on GT's does absoutly nothing!<BR>The only places where the snow was moved was at the extreme tips and what looked like a little melting from the decklid vents||||reg||1
